1. प्रथ् cl. 1. Ā. (Dhātup. xix, 3) प्र॑थते (rarely P. ˚ति, e.g. impf. 2. du. अ॑प्रथतम्, RV.; Impv. प्रथन्तु, VS.; pf. पप्रथतुः, BhP.; mostly Ā. pf. पप्रथे॑, p. पप्रथान॑, RV.; aor. प्रथिष्ट, p. प्रथान॑, ib.; fut. प्रथिष्यते, प्रथिता Gr.),
to spread, extend (intrans.; P. trans. and intrans.), become larger or wider, increase, RV. &c. &c.;
to spread abroad (as a name, rumour &c.), become known or celebrated, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to come to light, appear, arise, Kir.; Rājat.;
to occur (to the mind), Rājat. :
Caus. प्रथ॑यति (rarely ˚ते; aor. अपप्रथत्, Pāṇ. vii, 4, 95; Subj. पप्र॑थत्, RV.; पप्रथन्त, ib.; प्र॑थयि, TS.),
to spread, extend, increase, RV. &c. &c. (प्रथयति-तराम्, Ratnāv. iv, 3; Ā. intr. RV.; AV.);
to spread abroad, proclaim, celebrate, R.; Hariv.; BhP.;
to unfold, disclose, reveal, show, Kāv.; Pur.;
to extend over i.e. shine upon, give light to (acc.), RV. iii, 14, 4.

प्रथम—ज॑ or प्रथम—जा॑, mfn. firstborn, a firstling;
 original, primary, RV. &c. &c.;
 (-ज), being the issue of the first (i.e. f˚-mentioned) marriage, Yājñ.

